==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ʌtʃə(r)}}

===Etymology===
From {{term|touch}}, the second sense being derived from to {{term|touch}} someone for money.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[touches]].
# {{context|Geordie|pejorative}} [[toucha]]; one who tries get something out of others for nothing in return.

===Anagrams===
* [[retouch#English|retouch]]

----

==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{term|toucher|lang=frm}}, {{term|touchier|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term|tochier|||lang=fro}} (compare French doublet {{term|toquer|||lang=fr}} "to offend"), from unattested {{etyl|VL.|fr}} *{{term||toccāre|to knock, strike, offend|lang=la}}, of {{etyl|gem|fr}} origin, from Old Low {{etyl|frk|fr}} *{{term||tokkōn, *tukkōn|to touch|lang=frk}}, from {{proto|Germanic|tukkōnan||tukkijanan|to jerk, knock, strike, offend|lang=fr}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|dewk-|to lead, pull, draw|lang=fr}}, influenced by proximity to similar forms from {{proto|Germanic|tēkanan|to touch|lang=fr}}. Cognate with {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|zochhon|zochhōn|to grasp, seize|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|zuchon|zuchôn|to jerk, tug|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|tucken|tucken|to tug|lang=gmh}}, {{etyl|odt|-}} {{term|tocken|lang=odt}}, {{term|tucken||to touch, entise|lang=odt}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|tucian|lang=ang}}, {{term|tucian|tūcian|to mistreat, disturb, torment|lang=ang}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|𐍄𐌴𐌺𐌰𐌽||to touch|tr=tekan|lang=got|sc=Goth}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|taka||to touch grasp|lang=non}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|tacan|tacan|to touch, take|lang=ang}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tu.ʃe/|lang=fr}}, {{X-SAMPA|/tu.Se/}}
* {{audio|Fr-toucher.ogg|Audio (France, Paris)}}
* {{rhymes|e|lang=fr}}
* {{exthomophones|touchai|touché|touchée|touchées|touchers|touchés|touchez|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# The act of [[touching]] {{qualifier|see below}}.
# A way of touching.
# The sense of [[touch]], [[tactility]].

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# {{transitive|lang=fr}} To [[touch]] (physically).
#: ''Ne me '''touche''' pas !''
#:: ''Don't touch me!''
# {{transitive|lang=fr}} To [[move]] (emotionally).
# {{transitive|lang=fr}} To [[affect]]
#: ''La maladie '''touche''' actuellement 2 millions de personnes.''
#:: ''The disease currently affects 2 million people.''
# {{intransitive|followed by "[[à#French|à]]"|lang=fr}} To [[try]], to [[try out]].
#: ''Je n'ai jamais '''touché''' au tabac''
#:: ''I've never tried tobacco''
# {{intransitive|lang=fr}} {{colloquial|lang=fr}} Short for [[toucher sa bille]]. To be skillful.
#: ''Ce mec est un ancien critique d'art. Je peux te dire qu'il '''touche''' en peinture !''
#:: ''This guy is a former art critic. Believe me, he knows a thing or two about painting!''
# {{transitive|lang=fr|money, income}} to [[receive]], to [[get]]
====Conjugation====
{{fr-conj-er|touch|avoir}}

====Descendants====
* Dutch: [[toucheren]]

